---
description: Aangan dates use the floor calendar, and the clock only when the value has a time
alwaysApply: true
---

# Calendar

A date uses the floor calendar. Do not add `input type="date"`, `datetime-local`, or a native time box.

The closed control is `input.when-field`: 48px, line-height 46px, radius 14px, paper, chevron on the right. Text sits in the vertical middle. On a toolbar, align the field with the other 48px controls (`align-items: end`), not with the caption above it.

The open card is `.when-panel`. Days are Monday-first. Today has a saffron ring. The selected day is `#3d2b22` with cream text. Hover is `#f6efe4`.

Add `.clock` (hour, minute, AM/PM) only when the saved value includes a time, as on Show bookings at. A service date, leave date, or day filter is the calendar alone — no Time heading and no clock. A time with no date is the clock alone. Close on an outside click and on Escape. Keep the styles in `client/src/styles.scss`.

```html
<span class="when" [class.open]="open()" (click)="onWhenClick($event)">
  <input class="when-field" readonly [value]="label()" />
  @if (open()) {
    <div class="when-panel">
      <!-- month head and .cal-grid -->
      @if (withTime) {
        <p class="fine">Time</p>
        <div class="clock"><!-- hour, minute, AM/PM --></div>
      }
    </div>
  }
</span>
```
